    "description": "Payment service providers connect merchants to electronic payment services through terminals, online gateways, and supporting systems. Iranian provider documentation illustrates how this work extends from accepting a payment to reporting transactions and resolving discrepancies.",
    "tags": ["Electronic payments", "Merchant services", "Payment infrastructure", "Iranian business"],
    "status": null,
    "editorial_status": "needs_research",
    "as_of_date": "2026-10-26",
    "created_at": "2026-10-27T18:34:41Z",
    "updated_at": "2026-10-27T18:34:41Z",
    "seo": {
      "title": "Payment Service Providers in Iran | Iran, Unfolded",
      "description": "Understand Iranian payment service providers, their merchant services, and the distinction between providers, gateways, and terminal manufacturers."
    },
    "content": [
      {
        "id": "provider-role",
        "type": "text",
        "heading": "The company behind payment acceptance",
        "content": "A payment service provider, usually abbreviated PSP, brings together services that a merchant encounters through several different interfaces. Saman Electronic Payment Kish, trading as SEP, describes a business spanning physical card readers, internet payments, mobile payments, and cards. Its institutional profile identifies a dedicated payment switch, data-center infrastructure, monitoring, and a branch and representative network as parts of that operation. These are the company's descriptions of its infrastructure, rather than an independent assessment of service quality. [s1]\n\nThis makes the PSP a useful unit for understanding the industry: an online gateway is one service within a broader operational business. A provider's name on a terminal or payment page does not, by itself, identify the factory that manufactured the equipment. SEP's public service directory separately presents terminal installation and support, online gateway services, and merchant reporting. [s2]",
        "source_ids": ["s1", "s2"]
      },
      {
        "id": "merchant-operations",
        "type": "text",
        "heading": "What happens after a payment",
        "content": "The merchant relationship continues beyond checkout. SEP's public directory includes terminal transaction receipts, transaction reports, support requests, online-payment receipts, return receipts, and separate routes for investigating merchant-settlement, terminal, and internet-purchase discrepancies. These distinctions help explain why a receipt, a transaction record, and a settlement inquiry should not be treated as interchangeable documents. The directory demonstrates the available service categories; it does not establish how quickly individual cases are resolved. [s2]\n\nFor readers comparing this field with adjacent businesses, the important distinction is between the organization delivering payment services and the tools through which those services are accessed. A gateway provides an online acceptance interface; a terminal provides a physical one. The PSP's infrastructure and merchant operations support these channels. SEP's profile explicitly places internet gateways and card readers within the same service portfolio. [s1]",
        "source_ids": ["s1", "s2"]
      },
      {
        "id": "evidence-boundaries",
        "type": "text",
        "heading": "Reading provider claims carefully",
        "content": "Corporate profiles are valuable evidence of how providers describe their responsibilities. They are weaker evidence for comparative claims about reliability, security, or market leadership. SEP's profile combines descriptions of operational infrastructure with promotional assessments of its position, so this account retains the former without adopting the latter. [s1]\n\nA sector-wide assessment still requires a dated regulator directory, comparable transaction statistics, and independently examined operating results. This page therefore explains the provider role through a documented example and does not present an exhaustive licensing list or rank competing companies.",
        "source_ids": ["s1"]
      }
    ],
